        "reasoning": "We need P(D | X=+, Y=-). Use Bayes.\n\nLet D = defective. Prior P(D)=1/3, P(~D)=2/3.\n\nWe have conditional independent tests given D.\n\nP(X=+, Y=- | D) = P(X=+|D) * P(Y=-|D) = (3/4)*(1 - 2/3) = (3/4)*(1/3)=3/12=1/4.\n\nP(X=+, Y=- | ~D) = P(X=+|~D) * P(Y=-|~D) = (1/4)*(1 - 1/3) = (1/4)*(2/3)=2/12=1/6.\n\nNow posterior: P(D | evidence) = P(D)*likelihood / [P(D)*likelihood + P(~D)*likelihood2].\n\nCompute numerator: (1/3)*(1/4)=1/12.\n\nDenominator: 1/12 + (2/3)*(1/6) = 1/12 + (2/3)*(1/6)= (2/3)*(1/6)=2/18=1/9. So denominator = 1/12 + 1/9. LCM 36: 3/36 + 4/36 = 7/36.\n\nThus posterior = (1/12)/(7/36) = (1/12)*(36/7)=3/7.\n\nThus answer A.\n\nReturn A only.",
